-- Source module: Solutions.KIL4Step
/-!
# KIL4: one uniform Lemma 10 step with run-time parameters

`stepG k d neg pa pc stg` is a fixed program text built from *expressions*: `pa`, `pc` compute the
outer volumes `vol A`, `vol C`, and `stg` lists the (radix, control) expressions of the offset
table stages.  The expressions may read the modulus register `sQQ` and any descriptor register
(they must not read the parameter or stage stacks they are pushed onto).  The program

1. pushes the four size parameters and the stage list,
2. runs the uniform shift body `shFracU`,
3. pops the size parameters again (the stage stacks are consumed by the body).

`stepG_spec`: if the stages evaluate to a stage list `ac` whose table is the table of
`A.zip (csOf Λ c A)` and the volume expressions evaluate to `vol A`, `vol C`, the step replaces the
array on stack `0` by `shiftArr Λ i (fracU Q k d neg) c 0 xs` and leaves every other stack
unchanged.
-/

