`E_j = -Σ_{(c, k₁, k₂) ∈ T} c · bit_{k₁}(j) · bit_{k₂}(j)`: the mask bit (slot `h` of axis `i`)
times the linear form of the lower slots (`c = 2^{ℓ-h+t}`). This is a masked linear table.

* `svE Q M T`: one expression for `(-Σ c·bit·bit) mod Q` of the index in register `rN`
  (`bitE k = (j / 2^k) mod 2`); **`tabP`** loops over the records with a down-counter on `rN` and
  pushes the entries on stack `14`, ending with entry `0` on top (the layout `rotF` consumes).
* **`tabP_fsp`**: the table `(range N).map (fun j => (-tv T j) mod Q)`, cost
  `cLp N ((18|T| + 7)·10^7 (B+2)^2 + …) B` with `B = zsz U`, `U` bounding the index, the moduli,
  the coefficients and the sums. That is `O(|T| B²)` **per record**: `|T| ≤ D ℓ`, `B = O(log N + ℓ)`,
  so the bound is polylogarithmic per record and does not grow with the record length `r`.
* **`roundEx_slot`**: in any slot layout (`slotLayout hS`, in particular the paper's
  `paperLayout`) `roundEx … j = -tv (trips …) j`, so `sOf r (roundEx …) = tabEntry` with
  `Q = 2r`.
-/

